## Story Description
Three additions to the Supplier page table: (1) a concentration banner above the table showing what percentage of total spend the top N suppliers represent; (2) payment days colour coding on the avg_payment_days cell; (3) a WC opportunity column showing the per-supplier working capital opportunity using the same WACC=8% / target=45-day formula from the Payment Terms page.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/SupplierPage.tsx
- Concentration banner: between the search/group-by row and the table, add a div className='flex items-center gap-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground bg-muted/30 rounded-lg px-4 py-2'. Inside, compute: top5Spend = sorted.slice(0,5).reduce((s,r)=>s+(r.total_spend??0),0). top10Spend = sorted.slice(0,10).reduce((s,r)=>s+(r.total_spend??0),0). Render two spans: 'Top 5 suppliers: {formatPct(top5Spend/totalSupplierSpend*100)} of spend' and 'Top 10 suppliers: {formatPct(top10Spend/totalSupplierSpend*100)} of spend'. Guard: only render when totalSupplierSpend > 0 and sorted.length >= 5.
- Add a computeWc helper function at the top of the component (or file): const computeWc = (avgDays: number, spend: number) => avgDays < 45 ? ((45 - avgDays) / 365) * spend * 0.08 : 0
- Add 'WC Opp.' column to the columns array: { key: 'wc_opp', label: 'WC Opp.', align: 'right' }
- In the TableHeader, add a TableHead className='text-right' for 'WC Opp.' after the existing 'Avg Payment Days' column header (update colSpan references too)
- In each sorted TableRow (non-grouped): add a TableCell className='text-right' after avg_payment_days cell: const wc = computeWc(row.avg_payment_days ?? 0, row.total_spend ?? 0); render wc > 0 ? <span className='text-emerald-600 font-medium'>{formatCurrency(wc)}</span> : <span className='text-muted-foreground'>—</span>
- Payment days colour: in the avg_payment_days TableCell, replace the plain className with a dynamic one: avgDays < 30 ? 'text-right font-medium bg-rose-50 text-rose-700' : avgDays < 45 ? 'text-right font-medium bg-amber-50 text-amber-700' : 'text-right'. Apply to both grouped and non-grouped rows.
- Apply the same WC Opp. cell and payment days colouring to grouped supplier rows inside the expandedGroups section
- Update colSpan values in empty-state rows and group header rows to account for the new column (was 7, now 8)
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — zero TypeScript errors

